    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is Figma better than Sketch for most designers?</h3>
    <p>Figma is better for most design teams in 2026. Its browser-based collaboration, cross-platform support, and real-time multiplayer editing make it the default choice for product teams working remotely or across operating systems. Sketch is better for solo Mac designers who want native performance, a lower price, and a mature plugin ecosystem.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, Figma or Sketch?</h3>
    <p>Sketch is cheaper for individuals. Sketch costs $10 per editor per month or $120 per year, with a Mac-only license option. Figma Professional costs $12 per editor per month. For teams, Figma is more expensive but includes web-based collaboration that Sketch cannot match. Sketch is the better value for solo designers on Mac.</p>

    <h3>Does Sketch work on Windows?</h3>
    <p>No. Sketch is Mac-only and has no native Windows or web app. Designers on Windows must use Figma, Adobe XD, or other cross-platform tools. Sketch offers a web viewer for sharing designs, but editing is Mac-only. This is the single biggest reason teams switch from Sketch to Figma.</p>

    <h3>Which has better prototyping, Figma or Sketch?</h3>
    <p>Figma has better built-in prototyping. Its Prototype mode supports smart animate, interactive components, variables, and conditional logic without plugins. Sketch has prototyping through its native Prototype feature and the Sketch Cloud, but it is less powerful than Figma. For advanced prototypes, Figma is the clear winner.</p>

    <h3>Can I use Figma and Sketch together?</h3>
    <p>Yes, and some teams do. A common workflow is to use Sketch for solo design work on Mac, then export to Figma for team collaboration and handoff. Figma can import Sketch files directly, preserving layers and components. The combined cost is $22 per month, which is reasonable for designers who want native Mac performance plus web collaboration.</p>

    <h3>Which has a larger plugin ecosystem?</h3>
    <p>Sketch has a larger and more mature plugin ecosystem, with thousands of plugins built over a decade. Figma's plugin ecosystem is newer but growing fast, with official support since 2019. Sketch plugins tend to be more powerful for Mac-specific workflows, while Figma plugins are more focused on collaboration and developer handoff.</p>

